Hi all

Is it possible to obtain R2 values for all the levels of a grouping factor for a multivariate regression in Geomorph? For example, I'm looking at allometry with sex, age, and the year specimens were sampled as independent factors. I found age and year to be significant predictors so I would like to compare the allometric slopes (statistically and visually). Using advanced.procD.lm() I used the test for HOS to determine which levels in my factor were significantly different and now I would like to show the allometric slopes comparatively. Is it possible to do this? How do I obtain R2 values, slopes and intercepts for the levels within my each of my factors?

Any help in this regard would be appreciated

Candice

