Hi all,

I have a somewhat silly question. When running a 2-block PLS between a landmark dataset (shape3D) and a single variable (BF), does the order of the blocks matter?

I ask because the function runs smoothly with phylo.integration(BF, shape3D, tree_prune, iter=999)

but running phylo.integration(shape3D, BF , tree_prune, iter=999) leds to this error: Error in y %*% V : non-conformable arguments

I am trying to examine how cranial shape is associated with bite force (BF), essentially hoping to find a linear combination of shape variables that predicts BF. So I'm hoping to run a model that resembles BF ~ shape3D.

I greatly appreciate your help.

Best,
Chris

